<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40883" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-gĕro</span></b> , gessi,
			gestum, 3, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to bear</i>, <i>carry</i>,
			or <i>bring back</i> (freq. only after the Aug. per.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si summa terra sublata ex fundo meo et alia
					regesta esset,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					7, 4, 24 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terram e fossā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					44, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tellurem,</span>”
				<i>to throw back</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 11, 188</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humum,</span>”
				<i>to throw up</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					11, 3, 5</span></i>
			; cf. <i>subst.</i>: </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
